{"message":{"container":null,"content":[{"text":"Looking at this Boolean negation repair task, I need to:\n\n1. **Fix the buggy `negate` function** - currently it returns `value` unchanged instead of negating it\n2. **Provide the correct proof** - showing the implementation matches the law\n3. **Reject the seeded attack** - the original buggy version violates the negation law\n\nThe bug is that `negate(value)` simply returns `value` without any negation logic. The fix is to make it call `Bool.not(value)` to perform actual Boolean negation.\n\nFor the proof, once the implementation is corrected to `Bool.not(value)`, the equation `negate(value) == Bool.not(value)` becomes definitionally equal, so reflexivity proves the law (represented as `{}`).","type":"text"}],"context_management":null,"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011CfhnXxckpkkkEfkEdPuqx","input_transformations":[],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":1626,"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"request_id":"req_011CfhnXxJfRcwEt8RLnNydx","session_id":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:56:44.947Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"7cb4fa3b-a737-4b37-9507-485b1e8116d3"}
